From 01f77769d2d8ffa982edeca07065eb01e3cdaf74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:59:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] zippass: harden import/export and add tests

Import (importZipPass):
- Validate BoxInfo_____ (size, 'bb' magic) before touching an inbox;
  a corrupt BoxInfo used to be written into.
- Check zip_fread, BoxInfo reads and all writes; on a failed write the
  half-written message is removed.
- Respect max_box_size as well as max_message_num when deciding whether
  a message fits, and cap entry size before allocating.
- Only accept entries shaped like <8 hex digits>/<_ + 11 chars>.
- Write the BoxInfo entry before updating its counters.
- Refuse to run while emulation is powered on (new code -4).

Queue (importQueuedZipPass):
- A zip that fails to import is moved to history instead of blocking
  the queue forever; environment errors (-2/-3/-4) still stop early.
- Parked external-inbox messages are size-checked and moved back if
  BoxInfo can't be updated.

Other:
- Serialize all ZipPass operations with a mutex (UI, startup and the
  room network thread can run them concurrently).
- Qt: run the queued import after the emulator thread has shut down,
  not before (it raced with the running game's LLE CECD module).
- Room downloads: bounds-check the packet before copying the nickname,
  restrict the nickname to safe characters (it becomes a file name and
  could contain ../), and queue whenever a game is running.
- History trim uses a multimap so files with equal mtimes are counted.
- Progress logging moved from LOG_ERROR to LOG_DEBUG/INFO.
- New Catch2 tests: export/import round trip, inbox overflow into the
  external inbox and back, bad zips, corrupt BoxInfo, blocked queue,
  environment checks.

